Fall back to the configured data directory when dladdr() gives no directory.

libpocl finds its data (the kernel library bitcode in share/pocl) relative
to its own file, which it asks dladdr() for. When the loader knows the
library by a bare name only -- no directory in dli_fname -- the lookup
gave up and returned an error, although the configured directory
(POCL_INSTALL_PRIVATE_DATADIR) would have been right. On QNX fall back to
the configured directory in that case, as when relocation is disabled.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/lib/CL/pocl_util.c
+++ b/lib/CL/pocl_util.c
@@ -1992,6 +1992,12 @@
 {
 #ifdef ENABLE_RELOCATION
   const char *Path = pocl_dynlib_pathname ((void *)pocl_get_private_datadir);
+#ifdef __QNXNTO__
+  /* a name without a directory says nothing about where the library is:
+   * use the configured directory then */
+  if (Path && strchr (Path, POCL_PATH_SEPARATOR[0]) == NULL)
+    Path = NULL;
+#endif
   if (Path)
     {
       strncpy (private_datadir, Path, POCL_MAX_PATHNAME_LENGTH);
